---
description: Keep local, remote and release authority explicit
alwaysApply: true
---

Repository policy and the accepted task determine authority. Tier/model hints
never grant remote or irreversible action. Local reads, implementation and focused
checks may proceed within task scope. Feature push, merge, provider calls, mirror
delivery and release/deployment require their own explicit task authorization.
Review gates report evidence and do not confer authority. Preserve configured
policies and owner choices. Never infer a release permission from a green check.
